@prefix co: <http://purl.org/co/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix reg: <http://purl.org/linked-data/registry#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix vann: <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .
@prefix vs: <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

co:size a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has size"@en ;
    vann:example """
    :reading-list a co:Set ;
        co:element :paper-1 , 
                :paper-2 ;
        co:size "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .

    :citations a co:Bag ;
        co:item :citation-1 , 
                :citation-2 , 
                :citation-3 ;
        co:size "3"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
    """ ;
    rdfs:comment "The number of items belonging to a collection."@en ;
    rdfs:domain co:Collection ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy co: ;
    rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    vs:term_status reg:statusStable ;
    skos:note """
CO defines the size of a collection as the sum of the number of times entities that are part of the collection appear in it. This means that co:size considers how much each entity is involved by a particular collection, i.e.:
- the size of the set {a, b, c} is three;
- the size of the bag [a, a, b, b, b, c] is five;
- the size of the list (a, b, c, b, a, b, c, c) is seven."""@en .

